on-arrival: {!
Q.sikorski_marriage_bill_pending = 1;
Q.sikorski_marriage_veto_promised =
    Q.left_president || Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" ? 1 : 0;
Q.sikorski_repeal_stage = 3;
Q.sikorski_protest_strength += 10;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 28;
Q.rival_relation_ko_konf -= 12;
Q.minority_safety -= 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 16;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += -10;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 10;
Q.news_headline = Q.left_president
    ? "President " + Q.president_name + " promises to veto every repeal bill"
    : (Q.sikorski_marriage_veto_promised
        ? "President Trzaskowski promises to veto the marriage repeal"
        : "Trzaskowski leads KO liberals into the streets against Sikorski");
!}

= February 2027 — A rainbow inside the governing party

<span class="party-ko"><b>Rafał Trzaskowski</b></span> joins married couples, parents and equality
organisations outside the Sejm. He calls the repeal of marriage equality a
breach no democratic cabinet can launder by describing itself as temporary.

[? if left_president: Trzaskowski does not control the Palace. **President [+
president_name +]** does, and announces that every
repeal bill will be contested and vetoed. Sikorski's camp immediately begins
testing the label it hopes will stick: *the veto President*.?][? if not
left_president and president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": As President, he goes further:
he announces that the bill will be vetoed when it reaches the Palace. Sikorski
would then need three fifths of the Sejm with at least half of all deputies
present to override him.?][? if not left_president and president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski": He does
not control the Palace. His weapon is a revolt inside KO:
mayors, younger liberals and local councillors refuse the cabinet line while
their own party leader remains prime minister.?]

The first rainbow marches revive the movement politics of 2019,
but the adversary is now a cabinet elected by the same democratic parties that
once marched beside them. Police form double cordons: one around Parliament,
one between demonstrators and Konfederacja's counter-rally.

- @sikorski_marriage_join_2027
- @sikorski_marriage_left_line_2027
- @sikorski_marriage_legal_2027

@sikorski_marriage_join_2027
title: Join Trzaskowski's march without forgiving KO
subtitle: Defend the law together while keeping the constructive-vote ledger visible.
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 9; progressive_credibility += 5; minority_safety += 4; ko_relation += 2; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica and Trzaskowski share a march but not a coalition absolution"

We march, and we march behind our own banners rather than his. Trzaskowski
gets the crowd he called for and does not get a Left that has forgotten who
supplied the votes for the constructive motion that made Sikorski prime
minister.

Married couples on the pavement do not much care about the ledger and are glad
of the numbers. KO's organisers notice that our stewards are handing out a
leaflet with a division list on the back.

- @poland_event_queue: March behind our own banners

@sikorski_marriage_left_line_2027
title: Build an independent equality front
subtitle: Let KO fight itself while Lewica organises the people whose rights are at stake.
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 7; local_network += 3; progressive_credibility += 4; ko_relation -= 2; coalition_blur -= 4; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 12; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 11; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 9 if public_climate_progressive_index >= 48; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support -= 8 if public_climate_progressive_index < 48; news_headline = "An independent equality front refuses to become KO's internal faction"

We build the front out of the people the repeal actually reaches: the couples
whose registrations are in question, the registrars refusing to process the new
guidance, the lawyers who have been taking these cases since before KO
discovered the issue.

It is smaller than Trzaskowski's march and it belongs to us. His revolt becomes
one wing of a liberal party arguing with itself, while the organisation
defending the law is a Left organisation with its own address.

- @poland_event_queue: Build the front

@sikorski_marriage_legal_2027
title: Prepare the Palace and court briefs
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Turn Trzaskowski's objection into a constitutional defence of existing marriages.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party lacks a legal team for the national challenge.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; sikorski_legal_defence = 1; constitutional_restraint += 5; judicial_legitimacy += 3; sikorski_protest_strength += 4; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 6; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 6; news_headline = "Couples, mayors and constitutional lawyers prepare the marriage law's defence"

Constitutional lawyers and family-law practitioners spend the month turning the
objection into filings: what happens to a marriage already concluded, which
acquired rights survive a repeal, and where the Convention obliges the state to
protect them.

It will not fill a square. It is what a court reads when the square has gone
home, and it is the only instrument here that can still be working in
eighteen months.

- @poland_event_queue: Prepare the filings

@sikorski_trzaskowski_crosses_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — The crossing is bounded, the Palace stays out of party management and Razem's price is stated. Autonomy, platform and municipal routes now settle a real question: whether a famous arrival joins a party, conditions his entry, or is quietly prevented from owning the current he brought.
title: Rafał Trzaskowski joins [+ left_party_name +]
subtitle: The revolt over marriage equality becomes a permanent civic-progressive current inside the Left
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 53
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 3 and sikorski_nightmare = 1 and sikorski_refugee_wave = 0 and ko_seats > 0 and (sikorski_repeal_stage >= 3 or (sikorski_repeal_stage = 2 and sikorski_marriage_stage_before_repeal = 0))
on-arrival: {!
const trzaskowskiTransfer = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0)),
    24,
    Math.max(
        4,
        Math.round(
            (Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) *
            Math.min(
                0.24,
                0.10 +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) / 1000 +
                Math.max(0, Number(Q.sikorski_protest_strength) || 0) / 500
            )
        )
    )
);
Q.trzaskowski_joined_left = 1;
Q.left_trzaskowski_current_seats = trzaskowskiTransfer;
Q.trzaskowski_current_name = "Civic-progressive current";
Q.trzaskowski_affiliation = Q.trzaskowski_current_name +
    " in " + Q.left_party_name;
Q.ko_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) - trzaskowskiTransfer);
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + trzaskowskiTransfer;
Q.left_progressives_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) +
    trzaskowskiTransfer;
Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - trzaskowskiTransfer
);
Q.sikorski_refugee_seats += trzaskowskiTransfer;
Q.sikorski_refugee_wave = 1;
Q.sikorski_minority_government =
    Q.government_support_seats < 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.sikorski_government_status = Q.sikorski_minority_government
    ? "Minority cabinet surviving without 231 dependable votes"
    : "Constructive majority narrowed by the Trzaskowski exodus";
Q.coalition_status = Q.sikorski_government_status;
Q.progressives_strength += 8;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 8;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 6;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 18;
Q.news_headline = "Trzaskowski's civic-progressive camp joins " +
    Q.left_party_name;
!}

= March 2027 — The first refugees arrive with a leader

<span class="party-ko"><b>Rafał Trzaskowski</b></span> tells a hall of mayors, equality organisers and KO
deputies that a party governing through Konfederacja has abandoned the civic
coalition it claimed to lead. **[+ left_trzaskowski_current_seats +] KO MPs**
cross the chamber and enter **[+ left_party_name +]** as a named
civic-progressive current.

[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": The President remains formally
outside day-to-day party management. His political camp, staff network and
parliamentary allies make the transfer while he confines himself to the veto,
public argument and constitutional duties of the Palace.?][? if president_name
!= "Rafał Trzaskowski": Trzaskowski makes the break personally and accepts
that he will now organise inside a Left party rather than inherit KO.?]

This is not an endorsement or an electoral pact. The mandates change caucus,
the new current receives internal rights, and Sikorski loses the same number
of dependable votes. **[+ sikorski_government_status +].** The rest of KO calls
the crossing theft. iPL, Zieloni and the social wing of Poland 2050 begin their
own emergency meetings.

Razem accepts the equality fight and rejects the idea that it settles the
economic argument. Its delegation demands guarantees on progressive taxes,
public housing, trade-union power and public provision before former KO
liberals receive permanent influence over the Left's programme and lists.

- @sikorski_trz_autonomy_2027
- @sikorski_trz_platform_2027
- @sikorski_trz_municipal_2027

@sikorski_trz_autonomy_2027
title: Guarantee Trzaskowski a self-governing civic current
subtitle: Give the refugees their own congress and programme inside [+ left_party_name +].
on-arrival: trzaskowski_current_name = "Trzaskowski civic current"; progressive_credibility += 4; progressives_dissent += 3; barons_dissent += 4; razem_dissent += 4; razem_cooperation -= 2; coalition_blur += 2; news_headline = "The Trzaskowski current receives permanent autonomy inside the Left"

The refugees get their own congress, their own programme commission and the
right to disagree with ours in public. Trzaskowski signs because it is the only
offer that does not require him to disown five years of his own politics.

Razem reads the guarantee and asks the obvious question: whether a current that
may dissent on economics has joined a Left party or merely rented one. The
barons ask a shorter question about how many winnable places the new arrivals
expect.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the guarantee

@sikorski_trz_platform_2027
title: Bind the current to a common social and equality platform
subtitle: Make entry depend on labour rights, public services and the defence of enacted equality.
on-arrival: trzaskowski_current_name = "Civic-progressive current"; labor_credibility += 3; progressive_credibility += 3; party_unity += 3; razem_dissent -= 3; razem_cooperation += 2; coalition_blur -= 2; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 7; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 5; news_headline = "The civic refugees sign the Left's common social floor"

Entry is conditional. The current signs up to labour enforcement, public
provision and the defence of the equality laws before it receives a single
internal right, and the document is published so nobody can later claim a
private understanding.

Trzaskowski accepts terms he would not have accepted in any other month.
Sikorski's cabinet gave us the leverage; we have spent it on a platform rather
than on places, and the mayors arriving with him will discover which of those
they were promised.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the terms

@sikorski_trz_municipal_2027
title: Put mayors and local organisers before Trzaskowski
subtitle: Accept his camp while preventing one famous arrival from owning the entire current.
on-arrival: trzaskowski_current_name = "Municipal and equality current"; local_network += 5; movement_autonomy += 3; party_unity += 1; razem_dissent += 2; razem_cooperation -= 1; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "The new current is organised through mayors and equality networks"

The current is built around the mayors, councillors and municipal organisers
who came with him rather than around the man himself. Trzaskowski is its most
famous member and not its chair, and the internal elections are held quickly
enough that this is settled before anyone can argue.

He accepts with reasonable grace. His staff do not: several had assumed that a
national figure joining a smaller party arrives as its leader. What the Left
gains is a hundred functioning local organisations, and what it avoids is a
current that dissolves the day its founder is offered something better.

- @poland_event_queue: Hold the internal elections

@sikorski_black_march_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — The callbacks to Izabela and Dorota are earned and the veto/repeal distinction stays exact. Movement command, blockade and archive now cost different things: a mobilisation with no party logo, a capital that has stopped moving freight, or the one instrument here that still works after everyone goes home.
title: The black, rainbow and union spring
subtitle: The first repeal votes bring the protest movements of 2019 back under a harder security state
face-image: img/poland/events/womens-strike-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 54
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 4 and sikorski_nightmare = 1 and (sikorski_repeal_stage = 3 or (sikorski_repeal_stage = 2 and sikorski_marriage_stage_before_repeal = 0))
on-arrival: {!
const abortionAttacked = Q.sikorski_abortion_stage_before_repeal > 0;
const marriageAttacked = Q.sikorski_marriage_stage_before_repeal > 0;
const trzaskowskiPresident = Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski";
let leftVetoesThisMonth = 0;
if (abortionAttacked) {
    if (Q.left_president || trzaskowskiPresident) {
        Q.sikorski_abortion_vetoed = 1;
        if (Q.left_president) leftVetoesThisMonth += 1;
    } else {
        Q.abortion_reform_stage = 0;
        Q.abortion_reform_progress = 0;
        Q.abortion_law_enacted = 0;
    }
    Q.sikorski_clinical_death = 1;
}
if (marriageAttacked) {
    if (Q.sikorski_marriage_veto_promised) {
        Q.sikorski_marriage_vetoed = 1;
        if (Q.left_president) leftVetoesThisMonth += 1;
    } else {
        Q.marriage_reform_stage = 0;
        Q.marriage_reform_progress = 0;
        Q.partnership_sejm_passed = 0;
        Q.partnership_implementation_complete = 0;
        Q.partnership_revision_enacted = 0;
    }
}
if (leftVetoesThisMonth > 0) {
    Q.sikorski_left_veto_count += leftVetoesThisMonth;
    Q.sikorski_veto_president_branded =
        Q.sikorski_left_veto_count >= 2 ? 1 : 0;
    Q.left_poll = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) - 0.25 * leftVetoesThisMonth
    );
    Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.30 * leftVetoesThisMonth;
    Q.public_trust -= 2 * leftVetoesThisMonth;
}
Q.sikorski_repeal_stage = 4;
Q.sikorski_protest_strength += abortionAttacked ? 22 : 8;
Q.sikorski_police_militarisation += 2;
// 2024: the party chose what to say about Ostatnie Pokolenie's blockades.
// The escalating-penalty demand was answered then; the statute and the police
// practice it normalised are what the cabinet reaches for now, against a
// different crowd. The movements that were defended in 2024 turn out for us;
// the ones that were prosecuted do not forget who asked for the fines.
const protestRecord27 = String(Q.last_generation_stance || "");
const punitiveProtestRecord27 = Number(Q.last_generation_chain_stage) >= 2 &&
    ["Escalating penalties", "Decisive removal and civil damages",
        "Condemn and prosecute"].includes(protestRecord27);
const solidarityProtestRecord27 = Number(Q.last_generation_chain_stage) >= 2 &&
    ["Defend civil disobedience", "Solidarity with the blockade campaign",
        "Transport talks and monitored pause",
        "Parliamentary route for the demands"].includes(protestRecord27);
Q.sikorski_protest_law_precedent = punitiveProtestRecord27 ? 1 : 0;
Q.sikorski_protest_movement_ally = solidarityProtestRecord27 ? 1 : 0;
if (punitiveProtestRecord27) {
    Q.sikorski_police_militarisation += 2;
    Q.sikorski_protest_strength -= 7;
    Q.movement_autonomy -= 3;
    Q.feminist_trust -= 3;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
} else if (solidarityProtestRecord27) {
    Q.sikorski_protest_strength += 7;
    Q.movement_autonomy += 3;
    Q.climate_activist_support = (Number(Q.climate_activist_support) || 0) + 1;
    Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
}
Q.feminist_trust -= abortionAttacked ? 8 : 0;
Q.progressive_credibility -= marriageAttacked ? 5 : 0;
Q.minority_safety -= marriageAttacked && !Q.sikorski_marriage_vetoed ? 6 : 2;
Q.public_trust -= abortionAttacked ? 6 : 3;
Q.government_delivery -= 6;
Q.news_headline = leftVetoesThisMonth > 0
    ? "The Left President vetoes the repeal bills as Sikorski brands the Palace obstructionist"
    : (trzaskowskiPresident &&
        (Q.sikorski_abortion_vetoed || Q.sikorski_marriage_vetoed)
        ? (abortionAttacked && marriageAttacked
            ? "President Trzaskowski vetoes the abortion and marriage rollback"
            : (abortionAttacked
                ? "President Trzaskowski vetoes the abortion repeal"
                : "President Trzaskowski vetoes the marriage repeal"))
        : (abortionAttacked
            ? "A clinical death turns the repeal votes into a second Women's Strike"
            : "The marriage repeal fight fills the streets around Parliament"));
!}

= April 2027 — Not a reenactment, but the same machinery

[? if sikorski_clinical_death and not sikorski_abortion_vetoed: A pregnant patient dies after two hospitals
delay treatment while ministries withdraw guidance and Parliament restores the
old criminal risk. Her family asks that her name not become a party slogan.
The circumstances nevertheless recall Izabela, Dorota and the first Women's
Strike: clinicians waiting for legal safety while a patient runs out of time.?]
[? if sikorski_clinical_death and sikorski_abortion_vetoed: A pregnant patient
dies after two hospitals delay treatment while ministries withdraw guidance
and publicly dispute the protection still written into law. Her family asks
that her name not become a party slogan. The veto kept the reform statute;
administrative sabotage did not make clinical hesitation harmless.?]

[? if sikorski_abortion_vetoed: President **[+ president_name +]** vetoes the
abortion repeal. The reproductive-rights settlement remains law.?][? if
sikorski_abortion_stage_before_repeal > 0 and not sikorski_abortion_vetoed: The
reproductive-rights settlement is now formally repealed.?] [? if sikorski_marriage_vetoed:
President **[+ president_name +]** vetoes the marriage repeal as promised. Existing
marriages remain lawful while Sikorski begins searching for 276 override
votes.?][? if sikorski_marriage_stage_before_repeal > 0 and not
sikorski_marriage_vetoed: The marriage settlement is repealed alongside the
first package.?]

[? if sikorski_veto_president_branded: Government billboards, friendly
television panels and Konfederacja clips now repeat one title for **[+
president_name +]**: *the veto President*. The Left loses polling ground with
voters exhausted by institutional conflict even as both reforms survive.?]

Black umbrellas return. This time they are joined by hospital staff, rainbow
flags and union stewards from the frozen labour inspectorate. The government
declares Parliament and central ministries critical infrastructure. Police
bring armoured vans and water cannon; Military Gendarmerie units guard military
buildings and cabinet transport routes.

[? if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1: The ministry's legal basis is not
new. It is the escalating-penalty regime for repeat obstruction that this
party demanded against Ostatnie Pokolenie in 2024, applied by a cabinet that
had nothing to do with writing it. Interior lawyers cite our own statements in
the briefing note. The climate organisers who were prosecuted under it are on
the square today, and they are not standing near our banner.?]
[? if sikorski_protest_movement_ally = 1: The road-blockade organisers we
refused to abandon in 2024 arrive with legal observers, a medic rota and three
years of practice at being removed from carriageways. Nobody had to be
persuaded to come.?]

- @sikorski_black_autonomy_2027
- @sikorski_black_blockade_2027
- @sikorski_black_document_2027

@sikorski_black_autonomy_2027
title: Follow the Women's Strike's autonomous command
subtitle: Put legal aid and medics under movement control instead of party branding.
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 10; movement_autonomy += 6; feminist_trust += 5; local_network += 2; party_unity -= 1; sikorski_protest_strength += 6 if sikorski_protest_movement_ally = 1; movement_autonomy += 3 if sikorski_protest_movement_ally = 1; feminist_trust -= 4 if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1; sikorski_protest_strength -= 5 if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 10; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 9; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_backlash += 7; news_headline = "Lewica places its resources under the second Women's Strike's safety plan"

We supply the lawyers, the medics and the vans, and we take no decisions about
where the crowds go. The Women's Strike has been running this operation since
2020 and does not require a party to explain protest to it.

Our own press office finds it maddening: the largest mobilisation of the term
and no Lewica logo on any of it. Organisers who spent seven years watching
parties arrive at their marches with a stage and a list of speakers notice, and
remember.

[? if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1: Two of the coordinators were fined
under the repeat-obstruction regime we called for in 2024. They accept the
vans, allocate them to a district away from the main march, and do not put a
party lawyer on the legal-support rota. Solidarity offered late is still
solidarity; it is not the same as trust.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Send the lawyers and the vans

@sikorski_black_blockade_2027
title: Join the rolling blockades
subtitle: [? if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1: Escalate onto a road our own 2024 penalty regime now polices.?][? if sikorski_protest_law_precedent != 1: Escalate economic pressure and accept that the security apparatus will escalate with it.?]
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 16; workers_support += 5; party_unity += 3; public_trust -= 3; sikorski_police_militarisation += 2; sikorski_police_militarisation += 2 if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1; public_trust -= 3 if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1; progressive_credibility -= 4 if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1; sikorski_protest_strength += 6 if sikorski_protest_movement_ally = 1; news_headline = "Rolling blockades turn the repeal crisis into a confrontation with the state"

The marches become blockades — the ring road, the ministry district, the rail
junction at Warszawa Zachodnia — and the pressure stops being symbolic. A
government can ignore a square. It cannot ignore a capital that has stopped
moving freight.

The security response arrives with it, because that is what blockades produce.
Every water cannon and every mass detention is now partly ours, and the
argument about whether it was worth it will be settled by people who were not
on the road.

[? if sikorski_protest_law_precedent = 1: The detentions are processed under
the repeat-obstruction penalties this party demanded three years ago against a
climate group nobody was defending. Interior's spokesman quotes our 2024 press
release twice in one briefing, accurately, and the clip runs all week. We built
this road before we sat down on it.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Take the ring road

@sikorski_black_document_2027
title: Build a clinical and policing evidence archive
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Preserve hospital records, orders, detentions and injuries for courts and the election.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The documentation network cannot be maintained.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; sikorski_legal_defence = 1; media_capacity += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; sikorski_protest_strength += 5; news_headline = "Clinicians and observers preserve the record the cabinet wants fragmented"

Hospital records, deployment orders, detention logs and injury photographs go
into one archive with a chain of custody, built by people who assume it will
one day be disputed in court by a hostile ministry.

It is the least exciting decision available in a month like this one. It is
also the reason that, two years from now, somebody will be able to prove what
was ordered and by whom — which is not available to any of the people currently
shouting at the police line.

- @poland_event_queue: Open the archive

@sikorski_ko_currents_flee_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — Nowacka and every still-live KO current keep their boards, while an earlier Green dissolution is respected. Federation, separation and movement-vetted entry produce three different balances of power.
title: iPL follows Trzaskowski out
subtitle: KO's social flank chooses the refugee current over Sikorski's cabinet
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-chamber.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 55
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 5 and sikorski_nightmare = 1 and sikorski_refugee_wave = 1 and ko_seats > 0
on-arrival: {!
const iplRecord = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "ipl";
});
const greensRecord = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "greens";
});
let availableKoSeats = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0));
const iplTransfer = Math.min(
    availableKoSeats,
    Math.max(1, Math.round(Number(iplRecord && iplRecord.mp_count) || 5))
);
availableKoSeats -= iplTransfer;
const greenTransfer = Q.p2050_greens_absorbed
    ? 0
    : Math.min(
        availableKoSeats,
        Math.max(
            1,
            Math.round(Number(greensRecord && greensRecord.mp_count) || 3)
        )
    );
const koCurrentTransfer = iplTransfer + greenTransfer;
Q.ipl_joined_left = 1;
if (greenTransfer > 0) Q.greens_joined_left = 1;
Q.left_ipl_current_seats = iplTransfer;
Q.left_green_current_seats = greenTransfer;
Q.ko_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) - koCurrentTransfer);
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + koCurrentTransfer;
Q.left_progressives_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) +
    koCurrentTransfer;
Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - koCurrentTransfer
);
Q.sikorski_refugee_seats += koCurrentTransfer;
Q.sikorski_refugee_wave = 2;
Q.sikorski_minority_government =
    Q.government_support_seats < 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.sikorski_government_status = Q.sikorski_minority_government
    ? "Minority cabinet dependent on bill-by-bill PiS toleration"
    : "Constructive majority reduced to a narrow governing margin";
Q.coalition_status = Q.sikorski_government_status;
Q.progressives_strength += 6;
Q.climate_state_capacity += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 5;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 3;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 20;
if (Q.science_minister == "Barbara Nowacka") {
    Q.science_minister = "Sławomir Nitras";
    Q.science_minister_party = "KO";
}
for (const entry of [
    [iplRecord, iplTransfer, "internal iPL progressive current"],
    [greensRecord, greenTransfer, "internal Green current"]
]) {
    if (!entry[0] || entry[1] <= 0) continue;
    entry[0].bloc = "left";
    entry[0].kind = "current";
    entry[0].parent = Q.left_party_name;
    entry[0].legal_status = entry[2];
    entry[0].allied = 1;
    entry[0].mp_count = entry[1];
    entry[0].sejm_mps = entry[1];
    entry[0].exclusive_seats = 0;
}
Q.news_headline = greenTransfer > 0
    ? "Inicjatywa Polska and Zieloni enter " + Q.left_party_name
    : "Inicjatywa Polska enters " + Q.left_party_name;
!}

= May 2027 — The component parties choose their side

**Barbara Nowacka's Inicjatywa Polska** resigns its remaining government
posts and brings **[+ left_ipl_current_seats +] MPs** into **[+
left_party_name +]**.[? if left_green_current_seats > 0: **Zieloni** follow with **[+
left_green_current_seats +] MPs**, their climate and equality organisation,
and an insistence on remaining a recognisable Green current.?][? if
p2050_greens_absorbed: Zieloni cannot follow: the party dissolved into Poland
2050 in 2024 and its former MPs are no longer part of KO's seat ledger.?]

iPL does not dissolve. Its board, members and political debts cross into the
Left under written internal status.[? if left_green_current_seats > 0: Zieloni
do the same.?] Trzaskowski's arrival gave the refugees a door; the component
currents turn it into a corridor. **[+ sikorski_government_status +].**

Razem objects to admitting the former KO refugees without a binding social
floor. The dispute is now about candidate places,
taxation, housing and organised labour—not their shared defence of civil
rights.

- @sikorski_ko_federation_2027
- @sikorski_ko_separate_2027
- @sikorski_ko_movement_2027

@sikorski_ko_federation_2027
title: Form one progressive federation inside the party
subtitle: Give the admitted refugee currents a common council without merging them.
on-arrival: party_unity += 3; progressives_strength += 4; progressives_dissent -= 3; barons_dissent += 4; razem_dissent += 3; razem_cooperation -= 2; news_headline = "The refugee currents form a progressive federation inside the Left"

The admitted currents get one council, one convening chair and a rule that
disputes are settled there before they are settled in the newspapers. It is the
most administratively sensible arrangement and it creates, at a stroke, a bloc
inside the party larger than the old SLD apparatus.

The barons see that immediately. So does Razem, which points out that the
progressive federation and the socialist programme are not the same thing and
that only one of them now has a standing committee.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the council

@sikorski_ko_separate_2027
title: Guarantee separate internal currents
subtitle: Preserve each organisation and accept a more crowded internal veto structure.
on-arrival: movement_autonomy += 5; party_unity -= 1; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 4; razem_cooperation -= 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Each refugee organisation receives separate internal guarantees"

Each admitted organisation keeps its own boards, its own membership and its
own voice.[? if left_green_current_seats > 0: The Greens stay recognisably
Green;?] iPL keeps Nowacka's education network intact; Trzaskowski's people are
not asked to dissolve into anyone.

The party now has five internal bodies that can block a decision and no
mechanism for making them agree. Every list negotiation before the election
will pass through all of them, and the calendar does not have room for that.

- @poland_event_queue: Guarantee the currents

@sikorski_ko_movement_2027
title: Bind entry to the repeal movements
subtitle: Make climate, equality and municipal organisers answer to the social opposition rather than old KO hierarchies.
on-arrival: sikorski_protest_strength += 8; local_network += 4; climate_state_capacity += 3; razem_dissent -= 2; razem_cooperation += 2; coalition_blur -= 3; news_headline = "The former KO currents enter through the repeal movement's local councils"

Entry runs through the repeal movements rather than through the old KO
hierarchies: the climate organisers, the equality campaigns and the municipal
networks vouch for who comes in, and the former ministers arrive as members of
something rather than as a delegation.

It humiliates several people who were used to being negotiated with. It also
means that when the currents argue next year, they will argue in front of
organisers rather than in a room of former office-holders — which is the whole
point of doing it this way.

- @poland_event_queue: Let the organisers vouch

@sikorski_security_state_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — The strongest premise in the chapter, and the override count is honest about what a veto saves. Non-violence, general strike and campaign-pivot are now genuinely incommensurable: invisible discipline, the one instrument that can only be used once, or a documented record that feels like retreat.
title: The repeal state hardens
subtitle: The labour repeal reaches the Palace as militarised policing becomes the cabinet's answer to a summer of converging protests
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-sikorski.webp
